From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Remove the remaining 30/60 FPS gates, harden
 interpolation

Frame rate:
- The outer main loop (sub_821A9790) waited for a vblank whenever none had
  happened since its previous pass, capping the loop at the guest vblank
  rate (60 Hz). That wait is skipped now (821A9810).
- In a game, a loop pass only rendered if a tick ran, so at most 30 frames
  per second were drawn. Every pass now gets render reason 0x100, as in the
  menus (821A9524).
- Loading screens, drawn by the render thread while 82948F68 is 1, keep
  the original pacing.
- The frame-rate cap now waits at the start of the main loop body, before
  input is read, instead of after it.

Interpolation:
- The real state is restored at the start of the frame, so checkpoint
  saves, loads and map changes in the main loop body never see blended
  poses (the game_update entry restore stays as a fallback).
- Snapshots are only blended if no tick ran unseen between them (elapsed
  tick counter), so loads, reverts and ticks run by other drivers start
  over instead of blending stale poses into new objects.
- Object validity also checks the node block size and offset, teleports
  are also detected on the world-space root node (attached objects), and a
  blend factor of 0 draws the previous tick instead of the last one.

The main loop body entry hook is shared: pacing, then restore, then mouse
input.
